                  Yes. Equate, Walmart's store brand, sells a whey protein powder in a 24 oz tub of about 22 servings in vanilla and chocolate. Walmart's listing says it gives 24 g of protein per serving with whey isolate as the first ingredient. Walmart does not name the manufacturer, and we found no sport certification for it.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Is Equate protein powder good?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  On the label it looks like a normal, lean whey, very close to Optimum Nutrition Gold Standard on protein and calories, and it lands in the budget tier for cost per gram. The trade-offs are that the manufacturer is not named, we could not find a third-party sport certification, and it is only sold at Walmart rather than on Amazon.
                </p>
              </div>
