              <summary><h3>Which Walmart protein powder is third-party tested?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Muscle Milk Genuine's core flavors appear in the NSF Certified for Sport registry, which made it the only pick with a sport certification we could verify. Body Fortress carries an NSF Contents claim we could not confirm, and Six Star and Optimum Nutrition say they are banned-substance tested without naming a certifier on the pages we checked.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Is Walmart+ worth it for buying protein powder?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
