          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Walmart can be one of the cheapest places to buy protein powder, but only if you buy the right size of the right tub. The big tubs of Six Star and Body Fortress are the value plays, Gold Standard's 5 lb tub is the better-made everyday whey, and Muscle Milk Genuine is the one to choose if a verified sport certification matters. Equate's whey is a fair budget buy if your store has it.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you pick, ignore the front of the tub and the price per ounce. Work out cost per 25 g of protein from the panel, check who is selling it online, and compare against Amazon on the day. Powder is a convenient way to fill a protein gap, not the foundation of a diet.
